Cantera 3.2.0
===============

HUNDUN can optionally use a separately packaged Cantera 3.2.0 shared library.
Cantera is copyright California Institute of Technology, Sandia Corporation,
the Cantera Developers, and other contributors. Its BSD-3-Clause terms are in
LICENSES/cantera-BSD-3-Clause.txt. Licensor and contributor names may not be
used to endorse or promote HUNDUN-derived products without prior permission.

The verified package also carries notices for its compiled fmt, yaml-cpp,
SUNDIALS, Eigen, and Boost header closure. Those notices are installed from the
package's audited `licenses/` directory; Cantera's BSD license does not cover
those dependencies.

Chemical mechanisms and thermophysical datasets are separate copyright
objects. HUNDUN does not bundle a mechanism under the Cantera license, and no
mechanism is implied to be redistributable merely because Cantera can read it.

The Stage 4 Linux package prototype installs the complete audited license
directory beside one pinned shared-library generation. Its ABI manifest binds
that whole generation; replacing an individual shared object without replacing
the manifest and notices is unsupported.
